      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>This is Israel’s Zangwill’s versified English translation of the ofan piyyut of Shimon ben Yitsḥaq Abun of Mainz as published in Arthur Davis and Herbert Adler’s <tei:hi rend="italic">Maḥzor Avodat Ohel Moed: Avodat Ḥag haShavuot</tei:hi> (1909), p. 149. Zangwill’s adapted translation has six stanzas opposite the piyyut’s five; for the second stanza, Zangwill provided two. To reflect this adaptation, we have separated that stanza in order to keep the source text set side-by-side with the translation. –Aharon Varady</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
